  "docText": [
    "SOLAR®",
    "Biamp Design System",
    "1.0",
    "Counter",
    "Description",
    "Numeric badge showing count or quantity. Pair with buttons, tabs, nav items, and inbox rows.",
    "Types",
    "regular    Neutral count. Default for most contexts.\ndanger     Urgent or unread. For counts demanding attention.\ninverted   On dark surfaces and inside primary buttons.",
    "States",
    "default, hover, disabled. Note: variant uses legacy `active` — will migrate to `pressed` per SOLAR state vocabulary on next revision.",
    "Labels & Content",
    "Whole numbers only. Cap at 99+ or 999+ for long counts.\nHide counter entirely when count is 0 — never show a literal '0'.\nUse danger only for counts that demand action — not for every unread count.",
    "Rules",
    "DO   Use danger only for true urgency (unread, overdue)\nDO   Hide at count = 0\nDO   Cap overflow as 99+\nDO   Place adjacent to anchor (button, tab)",
    "DON'T   Show a literal '0'\nDON'T   Use danger type for every notification\nDON'T   Float counter away from its anchor\nDON'T   Use decimals or non-integer values"
  ],
  "pageContext": null
